<title>FRANCE: U.S. is top source for Paris air cargo imports.</title>
<headline>U.S. is top source for Paris air cargo imports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States was the main country of origin for air cargo import traffic handled at the Paris airports in January 1997, Paris airport authority, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>The principal countries of origin for ADP imports in January 1997, with percentage change on January 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  United States	  10,863    down 1.7pct</p>
<p> 2  Canada		    1,842    down 22.3</p>
<p> 3  Japan		     1,839    up   51.4</p>
<p> 4  United Kingdom	  1,649    up    3.0</p>
<p> 5  India		     1,557    down 24.7</p>
<p> 6  Hong Kong		 1,516    up    3.7</p>
<p> 7  Germany		   1,245    up   31.7</p>
<p> 8  Senegal		   1,071    up   30.8</p>
<p> 9  Thailand		    992    up   42.2</p>
<p> 10 Italy			 816    down 10.1</p>
<p> 11 Singapore		   672    up   84.5</p>
<p> 12 China			 631    up   97.2</p>
<p> 13 Korea			 620    up   86.0</p>
<p> 14 Morocco		     615    down 37.1</p>
<p> 15 Kenya			 563    down 43.9</p>
<p> 16 Egypt			 538    up   40.0</p>
<p> 17 Switzerland		 481    up   29.0</p>
<p> 18 Argentina		   447    down 12.1</p>
<p> 19 United Arab Emirates    431    down 36.4</p>
<p> 20 Israel			412    up   27.4</p>
<p>    Total		    28,800 tonnes</p>
<p>*January 1997 import traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 40,350 tonnes, an increase of 1.9 percent on the same month last year, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show. - Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
